        <h2>General information</h2>
        <p>
            On May 25, 2018, the General Data Protection Regulation became applicable in the EU (GDPR).
            Privacy and lawful processing of data entrusted to us by our users is our priority. We meet the
            requirements provided for by law and we address the following information clause to you, in which
            we inform you about the manner and purpose for which personal data are processed and about your
            rights regarding the protection of personal data.
            <br /><br />
            You do not need to contact WellMate, just read the content below.
        </p>
        <h2>Information clause</h2>
        <p>
            In accordance with art. 13 section 1 and item 2 of the General Data Protection Regulation of April
            27, 2016 (hereinafter: GDPR) we provide below basic information regarding rules for the processing of
            personal data.
        </p>
        <h2>Information about the Administrator</h2>
        <p>
            The Administrator of your personal data is WellMate Sp. z o.o. with its
            registered office at ul. Elewatorska 9, 19-200 Grajewo, Tax no.: PL7191577049, KRS No: 0001046050.
            <br /><br />
            The data administrator can be contacted via email: <a
                href="mailto:rodo@wellmate.io">rodo@wellmate.io</a> or in writing at
            the address of the administrator's office with the note "Data protection".
        </p>
        <h2>Scope of processing</h2>
        <p>
            We process personal data you provide when creating an account, using the WellMate mobile application,
            contacting us, or visiting our website. This includes account information, health and wellness data
            you enter or sync into the app, a per-installation device identifier used for data synchronisation,
            application crash reports (technical diagnostics; trimmed of personal content),
            and usage data needed to deliver and improve our services.
        </p>
        <h2>Purpose of data processing</h2>
        <p>
            The collected personal data will be processed depending on the legal basis for processing, in order to:
        <ul class="list-icon list-icon-arrow list-icon-colored">
            <li>Provide the WellMate health assistant service, including food logging, nutrition tracking, activity
                monitoring, AI-powered analysis, and personalised wellness recommendations (in accordance with
                art. 6 par. 1 point b of the GDPR);</li>
            <li>Improve and personalise the app experience, including analysing how features are used and
                delivering targeted insights relevant to your health goals (in accordance with art. 6 par. 1
                point a GDPR);</li>
            <li>Send service-related communications, such as account notifications and product updates, to the
                e-mail address provided (in accordance with art. 6 par. 1 point a GDPR);</li>
            <li>Respond to contact form enquiries and customer support requests (in accordance with art. 6
                par. 1 point b of the GDPR).</li>
        </ul>
        </p>
        <h2>Health Data</h2>
        <p>
            WellMate is a health and wellness application. As part of delivering our core service, we collect,
            process, and store health-related data. This section explains what health data we collect, how we
            use it, and with whom it is shared.
        </p>
        <h4>What health data we collect</h4>
        <ul class="list-icon list-icon-arrow list-icon-colored">
            <li>Food and drink logs, including meal names, ingredients, and nutritional values (calories,
                proteins, carbohydrates, fats, sugars);</li>
            <li>Body weight records;</li>
            <li>Exercise and activity sessions (type, duration, distance) — optionally synced from
                Android Health Connect;</li>
            <li>Heart rate and step count data — optionally synced from Android Health Connect;</li>
            <li>Mood and activity journal entries;</li>
            <li>Meditation session records;</li>
            <li>Text messages and food photographs shared with the WellMate AI assistant.</li>
        </ul>
        <h4>How we use health data</h4>
        <ul class="list-icon list-icon-arrow list-icon-colored">
            <li>To provide personalised nutrition recommendations and meal plans;</li>
            <li>To track and display your wellness progress over time;</li>
            <li>To analyse food images and identify nutritional content using AI;</li>
            <li>To power the WellMate AI chat assistant with relevant context about your goals and history.</li>
        </ul>
        <h4>AI processing disclosure</h4>
        <p>
            When you use the AI chat feature or the food photo analysis feature, the content of your messages
            and/or food photographs is transmitted to third-party AI providers for processing. These providers
            act as data processors on our behalf:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-icon list-icon-arrow list-icon-colored">
            <li><strong>OpenAI</strong> — processes AI chat messages to generate responses.
                Privacy policy: <a href="https://openai.com/policies/privacy-policy" target="_blank">https://openai.com/policies/privacy-policy</a></li>
            <li><strong>Google (Gemini)</strong> — processes food photographs for nutritional analysis.
                Privacy policy: <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank">https://policies.google.com/privacy</a></li>
        </ul>
        <p>
            We do not share your health data with these providers for their own training or advertising purposes.
            Data is transmitted solely for the purpose of generating responses to your queries.
        </p>
        <h4>Authentication providers</h4>
        <p>
            When you choose to sign in with a third-party provider, the data necessary to
            perform that sign-in is shared with the provider you selected. This happens only
            when you tap the corresponding sign-in button — never before:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-icon list-icon-arrow list-icon-colored">
            <li><strong>Meta (Facebook Login)</strong> — receives the fact that you signed in to
                WellMate via Facebook and provides us your basic profile (name, e-mail).
                We have disabled Facebook advertising-identifier collection and automatic
                event logging; Facebook is used solely to obtain your login.
                Privacy policy: <a href="https://www.facebook.com/policy.php" target="_blank">https://www.facebook.com/policy.php</a></li>
            <li><strong>Google (Sign-in)</strong> — provides us your basic profile (name, e-mail)
                when you sign in with Google. Used solely for authentication.
                Privacy policy: <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank">https://policies.google.com/privacy</a></li>
            <li><strong>Apple (Sign in with Apple)</strong> — provides us your e-mail (or a private
                relay address) when you sign in with Apple. Used solely for authentication.
                Privacy policy: <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/" target="_blank">https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/</a></li>
        </ul>
        <h4>We do not sell your health data</h4>
        <p>
            WellMate does not sell, rent, or otherwise trade your health data to any third party for commercial
            purposes.
        </p>
        <h2>The nature of data processing</h2>
        <p>
        <ul class="list-icon list-icon-arrow list-icon-colored">
            <li>Personal data will be processed manually by authorised persons and in an automated manner
                using information technology systems designed for this purpose;</li>
            <li>Automated processing of personal data may include profiling to personalise health
                recommendations, wellness insights, and content within the WellMate application.</li>
        </ul>
        </p>
        <h2>Data processing period</h2>
        <p>
            Personal data processed for the purposes previously mentioned will be processed until termination of
            the service provided by WellMate to the data subject or until the consent is withdrawn.
        </p>
        <h2>Transfer of personal data outside the European Economic Area</h2>
        <p>
            Some of the third-party AI providers listed above (OpenAI, Google) may process data outside the
            European Economic Area. Where this occurs, we ensure that appropriate safeguards are in place in
            accordance with GDPR, including standard contractual clauses. All other personal data processed
            directly by WellMate is stored within the European Economic Area.
        </p>
        <h2>Rights of the subject of personal data</h2>
        <p>
        <ol class="p-l-15">
            <li class="p-l-5">
                The right to access your personal data, rectify, delete or limit processing;
            </li>
            <li class="p-l-5">
                The right to object to further processing, and in the event of consent for data processing to withdraw
                it at any time. Exercise of the revocation right does not affect the processing that took place until
                the consent was withdrawn. Consent may be withdrawn by sending an appropriate statement to the
                e-mail address indicated above;
            </li>
            <li class="p-l-5">
                The right to receive personal data provided to WellMate in a structured, commonly used,
                machine-readable format;
            </li>
            <li class="p-l-5">
                The right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory body dealing with the protection of personal data.
            </li>
        </ol>
        </p>
        <h2>Obligations of the personal data subject</h2>
        <p>
            Providing personal data is voluntary, however, it is a condition for the use of individual
            services indicated in this document by WellMate. If you withdraw consent, you
            will not be able to use the services indicated in this document.
        </p>

